<title>UK: Hermes takes stake in Pilot - paper.</title>
<headline>Hermes takes stake in Pilot - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British pension fund Hermes took an 8.3 percent stake in Pilot Investment Trust Plc, the smaller companies trust, which is trying to fend off a 46.9 million pound ($72.67 million) bid from Undervalued Assets Trust (UAT), the Financial Times said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the purchase is thought to be friendly and designed to help Pilot defend the UAT bid.</p>
<p>On Wednesday the Pilot panel of independent directors said it &quot;strongly recommended&quot; shareholders reject the UAT bid.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
<p>($1=0.6454 Pounds)</p>
